text:
I sang seated at Michael’s feet;
Mitra had closed his tent above us;
the King of kings slept on his radiant bed,
and in dreams we two wept for Israel,

when Tippoo rose in a burning cloud…
Three times vengeance had been cried to heaven;
he called my brother Gabriel from above,
and turned his bleeding eye toward Michael:

“Behold the wolf, the tiger, and the lion…
One is called Ibrahim, another Napoleon,
and the other Abd-el-Kader, roaring in gunpowder;

They bear Alaric’s sword, Attila’s saber…
My spear and my great sword are there too;
but the Roman Caesar has not stolen the thunderbolt.”
